<Id>XuiHtmlElement1</Id>
<Width>544.000000</Width>
<Height>312.000000</Height>
<Position>24.000000,56.000000,0.000000</Position>
<Text>&lt;font color="#000000" size=11&gt;

The &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Combo Box&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; control has two available styles to choose from.
One of them is a fixed set of items to choose from, and the other allows the user to input their own text.
This can be set using the 'ComboBoxStyle' property, and by choosing the appropriate &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Visual&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;.

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;font size=8&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;/font&gt;

&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width="4%"/&gt;
&lt;td width="3%" bgcolor="#808080"/&gt;
&lt;td width="86%" bgcolor="#808080"&gt;

&lt;font size=5&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;/font&gt;

&lt;font color="#FFFFFF" size=10&gt;

In XuiTool, &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Combo Boxes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; (as well as &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Lists&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;) pull their items from a common set that can be specified in the 'Tools &gt; Options' dialog, under the 'Default' tab.
Normally, the parent application is asked to provide a list of text descriptions and images for each list item... which would allow each &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Combo Box&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; to be populated with different information.

&lt;font size=5&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;/font&gt;

&lt;/font&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td width="3%" bgcolor="#808080"/&gt;
&lt;td width="4%"/&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
</Text>
</Properties>
</XuiHtmlElement>
